{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Remediation validated + process bug filed\n\n**`rebar review-plan` on the remediated epic: PASS, 0 blocking, 11 advisory** — a fresh\nattestation was signed. Note it immediately reads `stale-code` again (`det_floor.py` drifted\nwhen 35bc landed); that is the documented moving-base-ref behaviour, not a defect. The epic will\nneed one final `review-plan` at close time, once all children have landed and the tree is\nstable. Don't chase it before then — every child that lands re-stales it.\n\n**Process bug filed: `e7be-b985-c344-46f7` (creamy-cocksure-elkhound)** —\n*\"Plan review certified an epic whose acceptance criteria were mutually unsatisfiable\"*,\nlinked `discovered_from` this epic and `relates_to` 35bc and 2aa6.\n\nIt records all seven unsatisfiable criteria found across this epic and two children, with the\noriginal text and the specific text each contradicted, in four classes:\n\n- **A — intra-ticket contradiction:** an AC contradicting its own ticket's Scope or another AC in\n  the same document (epic AC1; 2aa6 AC1 vs its own AC6; 2aa6 AC3; 35bc AC3 vs 5f4d's AC1).\n- **B — contradiction with a generated artifact's mechanics:** epic AC5 demanded a file be\n  regenerated from a source containing X and contain no X.\n- **C — hard-coded count:** epic AC4 said \"the 108 store tickets\" while 0a8c's Scope says the set\n  is recomputed at run time; the real number was 106.\n- **D — unowned scope:** epic AC1 required clearing a file (`llm/completion.py:288`) that no\n  child story covered.\n\nThe bug also records that each was caught only mid-implementation, by the completion verifier, or\nby manual audit — never at plan review — and that each fix forced a re-review via\n`stale-material`. Per the operator's instruction it deliberately does NOT diagnose the\nplan-review process; a follow-up session owns that."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785019894244761001,"uuid":"38d755c2-4eac-4a27-83ce-c132ae93d76c"}